{
    "_comment": "Polygon coordinates are NORMALIZED (0.0-1.0) so the same layout scales to any camera resolution. 'default' applies to any camera not explicitly listed below. 'type' controls risk_engine.py behaviour: 'restricted' zones trigger risk escalation, 'monitored' zones are logged but not inherently risky. 'allowed_classes', if set, marks any other class found in the zone as a violation (e.g. a vehicle entering a pedestrian-only lane, or a pedestrian in a vehicle barrier zone). 'max_dwell_seconds', if set, causes a LOITERING/EXTENDED_DWELL event once a track has remained in the zone that long. 'max_objects', if set, causes an UNAUTHORIZED_ZONE_ENTRY/GROUP_INCURSION event once that many distinct tracks are in the zone at once. 'severity' is the zone's own baseline severity label (LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH) used purely for display/explanation.",
